,"lo":-77.084069,"d":1997},{"n":"NCB","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":18.411226,"lo":-77.080712,"d":2351,"h":"24/7"},{"n":"Green Grotto Caves","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.421068,"lo":-77.113884,"d":1603,"ds":"The Green Grotto Caves are show caves and a prominent tourist attraction on the north coast of Jamaica.","wpu":"Green Grotto Caves","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Jamaica_Discovery_Bay_Green_Grotto_Caves_2.jpg/960px-Jamaica_Discovery_Bay_Green_Grotto_Caves_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Reggae Beach","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":18.421496,"lo":-77.044094,"d":6323,"ds":"Reggae Beach was a 250-acre property which was located in Jamaica, midway between Ocho Rios and Oracabessa. In 2008, the Caribbean Urban Music Awards were presented at Reggae Beach, which were based on the votes of over 1.5 million Caribbean music fans worldwide. Award recipients present at the ceremony were Beenie Man, Sly and Robbie, and Spragga Benz.","wpu":"Reggae Beach","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Reggae_beach.jpg/960px-Reggae_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ocho Rios (Spanish for \"Eight Rivers\") (Jamaican Patois: Ochi) is a town in the parish of Saint Ann on the north coast of Jamaica, and is more widely referred to as Ochi by locals. Beginning as a sleepy fishing village, Ocho Rios has seen explosive growth in recent decades to become a popular tourist destination featuring duty-free shopping, a cruise-ship terminal, tourist attractions and several beaches and acclaimed resorts. In addition to being a port of call for cruise ships, Ocho Rios also hosts cargo ships at the Reynolds Pier for the exportation of sugar, limestone, and in the past, bauxite.","wpu":"Ocho Rios","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/JM-ocho_rios-hafen-01.jpg/960px-JM-ocho_rios-hafen-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}